{"id":"2026-11-22-REGN","date":"2026-11-22","ticker":"REGN","name":"Regeneron Pharmaceuticals","sector":"Health Care","industry":"Biotechnology","price":920.69,"price_date":"2026-11-20","timeframe_days":182,"headline":"Regeneron's sales growth doubled to 36% in the September quarter, earnings rose 70%, and the stock still trades at its usual earnings multiple","side":"long","timeframe":"About 6 months, through the next two quarterly reports","thesis":"Regeneron's revenue grew 36% from a year ago in the September quarter, up from 17% and 19% in the two quarters before, and adjusted earnings per share rose 70% to $20.07. Two drugs drive it. Dupixent, the eczema and asthma drug Regeneron shares with Sanofi, sold a record $6.5B worldwide, up 35%, and Regeneron's cut of the profit pushed collaboration revenue up 52% to $3.0B. EYLEA HD, the long-acting eye drug that was losing ground a year ago, grew 62% to about $700M, and doctors' unit demand rose 20% in one quarter. Even after a jump from about 808 to 961 on the October 30 report, the stock trades at 16.7 times earnings, right at its median of 16.8 since 2023, so the market is pricing the speed-up as if it will fade. Management also gave more to come: a $1B upfront payment from Sanofi lands in the December quarter, about $3B of buybacks this year, and an FDA decision on cemdisiran for myasthenia gravis was due in November.","wrong_if":"A close under 830 would give back most of the October 30 jump and break the 50-day average, so the move would be over. The idea is also wrong if EYLEA HD growth stalls in the December quarter (management guided about 10% above the September quarter) or if Dupixent growth falls back under 20%.","business":"Regeneron discovers and makes antibody drugs. Its biggest product is Dupixent, sold with Sanofi for eczema, asthma, COPD and other allergic diseases; Sanofi books the sales and Regeneron gets a share of the profit, which shows up as collaboration revenue. Regeneron sells its own drugs too: EYLEA and EYLEA HD, injections for eye diseases that can cause blindness, and Libtayo, a cancer drug now running at about $2.2B a year. It has a large pipeline in eye, blood, cancer, obesity and nerve diseases.","segments_note":"Collaboration revenue, mostly Regeneron's share of Dupixent profit, was $3.0B in the September quarter, up 52%, and growth has sped up four quarters running, from 23% to 52%. Net product sales, mostly EYLEA HD, EYLEA and Libtayo, were $1.8B, up 14%, after a 16% drop a year ago and near-flat growth in June. So both halves are speeding up at once. Collaboration revenue is now about 59% of the total.","growth_note":"Revenue was $5.1B, up 36%, against 17% in March and 19% in June. Operating margin was 40%. Adjusted earnings per share rose 70% to $20.07, the third quarter in a row of double-digit growth. Some of the jump is the Sanofi alliance resetting how profits are shared, so growth will be harder to match a year from now. Missing: the brief's guidance table is empty, so there is no full-year revenue or earnings range to compare against; management spoke only of small changes to cost guidance on the June call.","commentary":[{"point":"Revenue grew 36% and earnings per share 70%, the third straight quarter of double-digit growth.","speaker":"Leonard S. Schleifer, cofounder and CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Dupixent sold a record $6.5B worldwide, up 35% at steady exchange rates, with US sales of $5.1B up 40%. Newer uses such as COPD and chronic hives are adding growth.","speaker":"Marion McCourt, head of commercial","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"EYLEA HD sold about $700M, up 62%, and doctors' unit demand rose 20% from the June quarter. They expect December quarter sales about 10% above September and full-year growth over 50%.","speaker":"Marion McCourt, head of commercial","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"A $1B upfront payment from the expanded Sanofi deal will be booked in the December quarter, buybacks are about $3B this year, and research spending rises by a mid-teens percentage in 2027.","speaker":"Regeneron management","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Opened by calling it another quarter of strong performance, and described Libtayo as gaining momentum in both its clinical results and its sales.","speaker":"Leonard S. Schleifer, cofounder and CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said the largest brands hit new all-time highs and the team is excited about the wider Sanofi alliance. Declined to say much about launch plans for new drugs, but said that was a matter of timing.","speaker":"Marion McCourt, head of commercial","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Argued that Regeneron's record of picking outside drugs to license beats the industry's, a sign they plan to keep adding to the pipeline.","speaker":"George D. Yancopoulos, president and chief scientific officer","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"}],"tone_note":"The calls have grown steadily more upbeat. Net tone rose from 64 to 80 to 90 over the last three calls, and the answers to analysts scored 75, up 18 points, which matters because answers are less scripted. Management declined no questions. The word count is a rough gauge, but it matches the reading: they spoke with confidence about numbers that were already in hand.","technical_note":"The stock closed at 920.69, well above its 50-day average (829.76) and 200-day average (751.41), and both averages are rising. It jumped from about 808 to 961 after the October 30 report and has held between about 920 and 973 since. RSI is 57, so it is not stretched. Over six months it beat the S&P 500 by 55 points and health care stocks by 21. Volume over the last 20 days is 22% above normal, a sign buyers are still active. The 52-week high is 991.73.","valuation_note":"At 16.7 times trailing earnings, Regeneron sits at its median of 16.8 since 2023, and the 20th to 80th percentile range is 13.5 to 21.6. Earnings are growing much faster than usual, so an ordinary multiple on fast-rising earnings is the case for the stock. If earnings grow another 20% and the multiple holds, the price rises about 20%.","levels":{"entry_lo":890,"entry_hi":935,"stop":830,"target":1070,"note":"Buy between 890 and 935, the lower half of the range the stock has held since the October 30 jump. The stop at 830 sits at the 50-day average and about three daily ranges under the entry zone; a close there would undo most of the jump. The target of 1,070 is about 8% above the 52-week high of 991.73 and assumes the multiple stays near its median while earnings keep rising. From the posted price that is about $149 of upside for $91 of risk, or 1.6 to 1."},"risks":["Part of the earnings jump comes from the new Sanofi profit split, so growth rates will drop once that is a year old.","EYLEA faces copies (biosimilars) and rival long-acting eye drugs, and EYLEA HD has to keep winning patients to offset that.","Drug price rules in the US, including Medicare price talks and any tariff on drugs, could cut future sales.","Research spending rises by a mid-teens percentage in 2027, which will slow earnings growth if sales growth cools.","Not known from the brief: the full-year revenue and earnings guidance, the date of the next report, and whether the cemdisiran FDA decision has come out."],"catalysts":["The FDA decision on cemdisiran for generalized myasthenia gravis, which management expected in November.","The December quarter report, likely late January or early February 2027, which includes the $1B Sanofi upfront payment and the first EYLEA HD number against the 10% guide.","Sanofi's Dupixent sales report each quarter, which comes out before Regeneron's.","Interim data early in 2027 from a study in geographic atrophy, an eye disease that causes vision loss, and first results in 2027 from a trial of Lynozyfic against standard treatment in multiple myeloma."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-18","adj_eps_name":"Non-GAAP net income per share","quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2023Q4","end":"2023-12-31","rev":3434.3,"gm":84.9,"om":28.3,"nm":33.8,"eps":10.2,"adj_eps":11.86,"rev_yoy":0.6,"eps_yoy":-5.6},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q1","end":"2024-03-31","rev":3145,"gm":86.2,"om":23.9,"nm":23.0,"eps":6.27,"adj_eps":9.55,"rev_yoy":-0.5,"eps_yoy":-5.4},{"q":"Jun '24","id":"FY2024Q2","end":"2024-06-30","rev":3547.1,"gm":86.5,"om":30.2,"nm":40.4,"eps":12.41,"adj_eps":11.56,"rev_yoy":12.3,"eps_yoy":12.9},{"q":"Sep '24","id":"FY2024Q3","end":"2024-09-30","rev":3720.7,"gm":86.8,"om":31.7,"nm":36.0,"eps":11.54,"adj_eps":12.46,"rev_yoy":10.6,"eps_yoy":7.5},{"q":"Dec '24","id":"FY2024Q4","end":"2024-12-31","rev":3789.2,"gm":85.1,"om":26.1,"nm":24.2,"eps":8.08,"adj_eps":12.07,"rev_yoy":10.3,"eps_yoy":1.8},{"q":"Mar '25","id":"FY2025Q1","end":"2025-03-31","rev":3028.7,"gm":84.7,"om":19.5,"nm":26.7,"eps":7.27,"adj_eps":8.22,"rev_yoy":-3.7,"eps_yoy":-13.9},{"q":"Jun '25","id":"FY2025Q2","end":"2025-06-30","rev":3675.6,"gm":85.6,"om":29.4,"nm":37.9,"eps":12.81,"adj_eps":12.89,"rev_yoy":3.6,"eps_yoy":11.5},{"q":"Sep '25","id":"FY2025Q3","end":"2025-09-30","rev":3754.3,"gm":86.1,"om":27.3,"nm":38.9,"eps":13.62,"adj_eps":11.83,"rev_yoy":0.9,"eps_yoy":-5.1},{"q":"Dec '25","id":"FY2025Q4","end":"2025-12-31","rev":3884.3,"gm":84.9,"om":22.7,"nm":21.7,"eps":7.84,"adj_eps":11.44,"rev_yoy":2.5,"eps_yoy":-5.2},{"q":"Mar '26","id":"FY2026Q1","end":"2026-03-31","rev":3605.4,"gm":81.4,"om":17.8,"nm":20.2,"eps":6.75,"adj_eps":9.47,"rev_yoy":19.0,"eps_yoy":15.2},{"q":"Jun '26","id":"FY2026Q2","end":"2026-06-30","rev":4290.7,"gm":86.6,"om":30.1,"nm":30.2,"eps":12.23,"adj_eps":14.29,"rev_yoy":16.7,"eps_yoy":10.9},{"q":"Sep '26","id":"FY2026Q3","end":"2026-09-30","rev":5115.8,"gm":88.8,"om":40.0,"nm":38.1,"eps":18.45,"adj_eps":20.07,"rev_yoy":36.3,"eps_yoy":69.7}]},"segments":[{"label":"Revenue type","quarters":["Dec '23","Mar '24","Jun '24","Sep '24","Dec '24","Mar '25","Jun '25","Sep '25","Dec '25","Mar '26","Jun '26","Sep '26"],"